.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateFluxUpwindSaturationProducts (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es)"

.PP
accumulates FV volume terms and first-order terms=inter-FV fluxes The transport velocity values projected onto the facet normals and multiplied with the facet areas are multiplied with the upstream values of the transported variable at each facet integration point and accumulated into the solution \fBvector<double>\fP as the upstream weighted first-order fluxes\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
To assign the higher order fluxes, the method needs access to the current finite element and the associated FV stencil processor\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateHigherOrderFluxSaturationProducts (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es)"

.PP
higher-order version for the case when fractional flows are considered The transport velocity values projected onto the facet normals and multiplied with the facet areas are multiplied with the (limited) 'isat' variable values at each facet integration point to define the higher order fluxes\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
To assign the higher order fluxes, the method needs access to the current finite element and the associated FV stencil processor\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateHigherOrderRHS (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es)"

.PP
higher-order solution is added from RHS (first order in time) Higher-order fluxes are calculated from the slope-limited saturations at the current and previous time levels and the corresponding volume fluxes integrated over the facets dividing the finite-volume sectors\&. 
.br

.PP
The contributions from the two time levels are weighted using the theta limiter value computed for each facet\&. When theta=1 the scheme is fully implicit, i\&.e\&. only the contributions for the new time level are considered\&. Theta limiting attempts however the equally weight the contributions on the basis of their magnitude\&. If this is achieved, the scheme is second-order accurate in time and numerical diffusion is minimized\&. 
.br

.PP
The computed higher-order fluxes are subtracted from the righthand vector\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
To compute the higher-order fluxes, the method requires access to the current \fBElement\fP and up-to-date finite volume processor object\&. 
.br

.PP
The method requires the facet-fluxes and the slope-limited interpolated values of the transported variable at the facet integration points\&. The temporal limiter value, theta, is supplied as a 7th method argument\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
In higher-order theta-limited transport scheme\&. 
