.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateLHS (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es, double time_multiplier)"

.PP
FV volume terms in diagonal & first-order terms=inter-FV fluxes in off-diagonal\&. Accumulates the volume over the time-increment and the outgoing facet- integrated fluxes into the diagonal of the solution matrix\&. 
.br

.PP
An upstream coupling is created by accumulating the fluxes that come into the finite-volumes sectors as off-diagonal elements\&. For each finite-volume facet, there are the nodes i (inside) and j(outside)\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The current \fBElement\fP and uptodate FiniteVolumeProcessor are used to retrieve the variables of interest\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateRHS (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es, std::vector< double > & SAT0, double time_multiplier)"

.PP
for iterative computations Righthand side for Backward-Euler FD time stepping 
.br
 
.PP
.nf
RHS = (FV-volume * sat_t0) / time-increment

.fi
.PP
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The current \fBElement\fP and up-to-date FiniteVolumeProcessor are used to retrieve the variables of interest\&. The saturations from the current timelevel are supplied by the \fBvector<double>\fP SAT0\&. The time-multiplier is needed to divide the finite-volume sector volume by\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AccumulateSectorSourceTermsInLHS (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es)"
Source term per finite volume sector is added to the diagonal of the matrix\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::AddToRHS (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & es)"

.PP
first-order Backward Euler solution is added to RHS Add first-order Backward Euler solution to RHS (using upstream saturations)\&. This integrates upstream sats over the segments by summing (flux * saturation) products over faces\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
References to the current element, finite-volume stencil processor, and the fluxes integrated over the facets inside the current element\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> CSMP_DEFAULT_LINEAR_SOLVER * \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::GetSolver ()"
returns the solver object if SAMG is used to solve the matrix equations It is important to note that this, just like the old method above (GetSolverSettings), asks for an instance of \fBSAMG_Solver\fP that may not exist, given that if the problem is smaller than 50 nodes, a Gauss_Jordan solver is created by default\&. I believe this needs re-consideration\&. Rather , I would utilize \fBSAMG_Solver\fP even for small problems, with special settings\&. -- Julian 24-09\&.2013 
