.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeAlgorithm\fP< dim >::SubtractNonConservativeOutFluxesFromRHS (\fBTwoPhaseModel\fP< dim > & relperm, const std::vector< double > & FLUX_BALANCE, const \fBcsmp::Index\fP & ad_key)"
including potential point sources or sinks in the model\&.

.PP
If the fluxbalance is negative, this means that there is outflow from a truncated boundary cell that only has inward pointing normals\&.

.PP
This function compensates this negative balance\&.

.PP
